BT /F1 10 Tf 40 744 Td (Q1. [maths | Limits and continuity] What is lim\(x->0\) sin\(x\) / x ?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 729 Td (  A. 0) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 714 Td (  B. 1) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 699 Td (  C. inf) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 684 Td (  D. -1) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 669 Td (Answer: B) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 654 Td (  This is a standard limit. As x approaches 0, sin\(x\) behaves like x, so the ratio tends) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 639 Td (  to 1. It is the key limit behind the derivative of sin.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 624 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 609 Td (Q2. [maths | Derivatives] If f\(x\) = x? - 3x, what is f?\(1\)?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 594 Td (  A. 0) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 579 Td (  B. 3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 564 Td (  C. -2) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 549 Td (  D. 6) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 534 Td (Answer: A) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 519 Td (  Differentiate term by term: f?\(x\) = 3x? - 3. At x = 1, f?\(1\) = 3 - 3 = 0. The tangent is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 504 Td (  horizontal there.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 489 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 474 Td (Q3. [maths | Derivatives] What is the derivative of ln\(x? + 1\)?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 459 Td (  A. 1/\(x? + 1\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 444 Td (  B. 2x/\(x? + 1\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 429 Td (  C. 2x ln\(x? + 1\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 414 Td (  D. x/\(x? + 1\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 399 Td (Answer: B) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 384 Td (  Use the chain rule: d/dx ln\(u\) = u?/u with u = x? + 1. Since u? = 2x, the derivative is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 369 Td (  2x/\(x? + 1\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 354 Td () Tj ET
