BT /F1 10 Tf 40 294 Td (How to evaluate limits by substitution, factoring and conjugates, the standard limits to memorise, and what continuity means at a point.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 279 Td (Key points:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 264 Td (- Substitute first; only simplify when you meet 0/0 or inf/inf.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 249 Td (- Factor for polynomials, conjugate for square roots.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 234 Td (- Learn the four standard limits by heart.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 219 Td (- Continuity needs the value and both one-sided limits to agree.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 40 204 Td () Tj ET
